# Copilot likes tables, and Telegram has no table markup: a monospace block wraps on a
# phone into something unreadable. So a notification's tables are sent as pictures with
# the table drawn in them, each between the paragraphs it was written between.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_telegram private
session existing-app Existing app session

wait_for Existing app session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling

# What the session said: prose, a table, more prose. The stub reads \n as a line break.
type e2e:work 1500 Here are the **results**:\n\n| Name | Size | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| alpha | 12 KB | ok |\n| beta | 3 MB | failed |\n\nShall I retry beta?
press enter
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session

telegram_wait Here are the <b>results</b>:
telegram_wait photo
telegram_wait Shall I retry beta?
telegram_expect_not <pre>
telegram_expect_not Table 1
# The prose before, the picture, the prose after: the order the session wrote.
telegram_order Here are the <b>results</b>: || photo || Shall I retry beta?
telegram_dump 01-table-sent
